{
  "uid": "weather-app-obs",
  "title": "Weather App \u2014 Observability",
  "tags": [
    "weather-app",
    "lab"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "editable": true,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-1h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Application",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Error rate",
      "description": "5xx responses as a share of all requests. The alert threshold is 5%. `or vector(0)` makes an absent 5xx series read as zero rather than No data.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "(sum(rate(flask_http_request_total{status=~\"5..\"}[5m])) or vector(0)) / clamp_min(sum(rate(flask_http_request_total[5m])), 0.0001)",
          "legendFormat": "5xx share",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.05
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "graphMode": "area",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Requests / sec",
      "description": "Throughput. rate() over a counter, averaged across 5 minutes.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 6,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(flask_http_request_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "req/s",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "graphMode": "area",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Requests per second by status",
      "description": "Splitting by status separates healthy traffic from 4xx and 5xx.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(rate(flask_http_request_total[5m])) by (status)",
          "legendFormat": "{{status}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Request latency percentiles",
      "description": "Percentiles, not the average: an average hides the slow tail that users actually feel. The alert fires on p95 above 1s.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum(rate(flask_http_request_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])) by (le))",
          "legendFormat": "p50",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum(rate(flask_http_request_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])) by (le))",
          "legendFormat": "p95",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum(rate(flask_http_request_duration_seconds_bucket[5m])) by (le))",
          "legendFormat": "p99",
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Targets up",
      "description": "How many scrape targets are responding. Expect 7. A drop means an exporter stopped or a security group changed.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 6
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "sum(up)",
          "legendFormat": "targets",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 7
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "graphMode": "area",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "justifyMode": "auto"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Hosts",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 13
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "CPU used %",
      "description": "Derived from idle time: 100 minus the idle share is what is in use.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 14
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "100 - (avg by (instance) (rate(node_cpu_seconds_total{mode=\"idle\"}[5m])) * 100)",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Memory used %",
      "description": "MemAvailable, not MemFree: Linux uses free memory for cache, so MemFree understates what an application could actually claim.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 14
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "100 * (1 - node_memory_MemAvailable_bytes / node_memory_MemTotal_bytes)",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Root disk used %",
      "description": "Root filesystem only. Docker images and logs are the usual cause of growth.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 14
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
          },
          "expr": "100 * (1 - node_filesystem_avail_bytes{mountpoint=\"/\"} / node_filesystem_size_bytes{mountpoint=\"/\"})",
          "legendFormat": "{{instance}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percent",
          "custom": {
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never"
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "mean",
            "max"
          ]
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Traces",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 21
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Slowest traces (over 300ms)",
      "description": "Traces slower than the alert threshold, newest first. This is the jump from symptom to cause: a latency alert names a time window, these are the individual requests inside it. Click a trace ID to open the span tree in Jaeger.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "jaeger",
        "uid": "jaeger"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 22
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "jaeger",
            "uid": "jaeger"
          },
          "queryType": "search",
          "service": "weather-app",
          "operation": "",
          "tags": "",
          "minDuration": "300ms",
          "limit": 20,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "showHeader": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 22,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Traces with errors",
      "description": "Traces whose spans carry error=true, which OpenTelemetry sets on a 5xx response. Open one and the span tree shows which call failed; its trace_id matches the JSON log lines in CloudWatch.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "jaeger",
        "uid": "jaeger"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 22
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "jaeger",
            "uid": "jaeger"
          },
          "queryType": "search",
          "service": "weather-app",
          "operation": "",
          "tags": "error=true",
          "limit": 20,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {},
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "showHeader": true
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 23,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Alert to trace to log",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 31
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**1. Alert** fires in Discord with the rule name and value.  \n**2. Trace** \u2014 find the offending request in the tables above, or in [Jaeger](/explore), filtered to the alert's time window.  \n**3. Log** \u2014 copy the `trace_id` from the trace and search CloudWatch:  \n`aws logs filter-log-events --log-group-name /weather-app/web --filter-pattern '\"<trace_id>\"'`  \n\nMetrics carry no trace ID by design: a metric is an aggregate, and a per-request label would create one series per request. The join runs metric to time window to trace to log."
      }
    }
  ],
  "links": [
    {
      "title": "Jaeger",
      "type": "link",
      "icon": "external link",
      "url": "http://${__url_time_range}",
      "targetBlank": true,
      "tooltip": "Open Jaeger to search traces"
    }
  ]
}